a heart surgeon took his car to his  local garage for a regular service where  he usually exchanged the friendly banter  with the owner a skilled mechanic so  tell me says the mechanic i've been  wondering about what we both do for a  living and how much more you get paid  than me yes as the surgeon well look at  this says the mechanic as he worked on a  big complicated engine i check how it's  running open it up fix the valves put it  all back together so it works good as  new we basically do the same job but  don't we and yet you get paid way more  than me how do you explain that the  surgeon thought for a moment smiled and  replied  try it with the engine running  differences in perception are present  throughout our everyday interactions the  instance with the doctor and the  mechanic was picked just to illustrate  how people can interpret different life  experiences based on their own  perception and understanding of the  world most of our problems in our  everyday endeavors stem from our  inability to understand the power of  perception and how this can affect one's  life and experiences i like to call  those problems problems of perception  and their typical consequences include  the feeling of disappointment and being  let down by others  getting into disagreements and verbal  fights  experiencing disconnection and isolation  accusing others of being responsible for  your own problems such issues can have a  detrimental effect on our psychology  it's not a small thing to have to deal  with a lack of sync in the majority of  human interactions you encounter it can  lead to frustration anxiety anger lack  of motivation and depression and that's  the reason i decided to cover the  concept of perception in this video in  our attempts to pursue a lasting effect  of abundance in our lives understanding  perception can become an invaluable tool  in our mental toolbox  remember the infamous blue and black  dress that tore the internet apart some  years ago although it was confirmed that  the color of the dress was blue and  black a lot of people saw the dress as  white and gold this was quite an  interesting visual phenomenon that  signifies to a huge extent the power of  perception in our everyday lives because  of different processes that take place  in the brain of each individual the way  we perceive things compared to others  may vary significantly even the  slightest difference in perception that  is caused by let's say an insignificant  dress can cause debate and in some cases  even arguments between individuals who  just want to prove themselves right the  way that things look feel smell taste  and sound is not necessarily the way  they really are though things may appear  to be color to us our experiences of  color are merely representative of the  surface properties of objects the  physical property of reflecting certain  wavelengths of light and the color red  as we experience it are two quite  different things in our attempt however  to justify our perceptual thinking what  we fail to recognize is that perception  is molding our reality and especially  the quality of our relationships through  problems of perception we fail to grasp  the essence of the world around us we  constantly communicate with other people  but we rarely understand them but how  can you really try and understand  another person if you are constantly  limited by the narrow boundaries that  your own perception dictates this  process can only be achieved by  initiating a perceptual shift a shift  that will gradually disengage you from  your own perception and give you the  incredibly powerful ability to see the  world through the eyes of others while  doing some research on the topic of  perception i stumbled upon a mindfulness  coach named shelly tigielski her views  on the topic are quite enlightening  the world is an idea more specifically  the world is your idea this sentence  didn't come to me organically it was  first expressed by the great 19th  century philosopher arthur soppenhauer  in his seminal work the world as will  and representation  no truth is more absolutely certain than  that all that exists for knowledge and  therefore this whole world is only  objects in relation to subject  perception of a perceiver in a word idea  the world his idea if only he knew that  after almost two centuries his writings  would have such a huge impact on the way  that we communicate and shape our  relationships whenever people have  arguments they usually lose touch with  reality because they get caught up in  their idea of the world when we fight  with others we hear our perception of  others words gestures and so forth we  make meaning out of what others  communicate based on that this may or  may not match the meaning they tend to  convey if i am offended by others it is  important to understand that i am  actually offended by what i do with  their words based on how i made meaning  out of them in essence i am offended by  them in me not by them the real person i  can never experience them the real  person directly in the end i'm offended  by none other than myself in short it is  not what people do to me that causes  problems for me but what i do with  people to cause myself problems the  power of reframing is unquestionable for  instance when somebody insults me  instead of thinking  x told me i'm bad at y  i can reframe this into i had x in me  telling me that i'm bad at why this  change in perception of how you  experience other opinions instantly  helps you release tension with reframing  when you respond to the person you are  responding to your perception you are  responding to you there are huge  benefits to understanding and  communicating with this in mind when i  really get this principle a whole new  world in me opens up  suddenly i don't take things personally  i do not get offended very easily i can  listen to criticism with an open mind i  don't take myself so seriously or  believe that others have power over me  a common issue when it comes to  perception is that we usually act  passively and not actively to the  processes we experience we tend to  victimize ourselves when people interact  with us in a negative way she made me  feel so angry my father makes me feel  helpless i'm troubled by my past in  reality i am the one doing the acting  i actively create my own experience with  perceptual change i express myself  differently i anger myself with hair i  make myself feel helpless when i am with  my father i travel myself with my past  this way of putting words together  suggests that i'm an active participant  in my own experience  i'm doing things to myself as opposed to  having things done to me the difference  between i am troubled by my past and i  travel myself with my past is huge there  is a clear lack of responsibility in the  first sentence whereas the second  communicates a person that is  characterized by self-reliance  self-reliance allows you to act upon  your problem  you change from the victim to the person  in control  and control is the bedrock of  self-ownership  when we work with our perception and the  things we experience we think that we  are experiencing a combination of past  present and future acts that's not true  now is all we have you are experiencing  yourself in the now and past and future  are just parameters that distort the  idea of now especially when we speak  about the past and the future we fail to  recognize that we do it within the  premise of now when you say for instance  tomorrow is going to be a scary day this  becomes i scare myself with my thoughts  about tomorrow or my parents mistreated  me when i was a child this becomes i  trouble myself now with thoughts of  being mistreated when i was a child  so the world i interact with is within  me i actively create it right now  perceptual change makes this healing  concepts a reality after experimenting  with it for quite some time i came to  understand that when others judge me i  am actually using my perception of them  to judge myself i also realized that  what others refer to is just their  perception of me not me perception forms  the foundation of our world when we  change the structure of our perception  we change the structure of our  world hey guys hope you enjoyed today's  video if you did make sure to like  subscribe turn on notifications and  comment below something cool please so  that more people can discover it  if you want to watch more videos from my  channel check out this one and this one  take care see you soon adrian out
 

